# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000060  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured so changes made to the level and
# type of log records stored in the centralized repository must take effect
# immediately without the need to reboot or restart the application.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000060
group:           V-241820
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366 CCI-001914
control_rev5:    AU-12 CM-6

contribution:    Splunk binds a configuration file to a reload handler through the app.conf
                 [triggers] stanza, which is the product's own mechanism for applying a
                 change in place instead of restarting; the application's share is that the
                 files governing the level and type of records stored are bound to a reload
                 rather than marked as requiring a restart.

governs:         app.conf - Settings for an installed app: whether it is enabled, visible, and what it
                 may do.

check:           app.conf [triggers] reload.audit not_equals never
check:           app.conf [triggers] reload.inputs not_equals never
check:           app.conf [triggers] reload.props not_equals never
check:           app.conf [triggers] reload.transforms not_equals never

external:        Settings whose own specification states that a restart is required -
                 indexes.conf coldToFrozenDir is one, per indexes.conf.spec:800 - cannot be
                 applied in place by any configuration, so for those settings the remainder
                 of the objective rests on the site's change management procedure rather
                 than on Splunk.
external:        A configuration change pushed from a deployment server or cluster manager
                 reaches this instance on that component's own schedule, which is outside
                 this instance's configuration.
external:        Product STIG SPLK-CL-000270 and SPLK-CL-000290, attached through this
                 requirement's CCI set, direct changes to inputs.conf and outputs.conf on
                 the indexer, forwarder and search head; where those are separate instances
                 their configuration is assessed on those instances.

citation:        app.conf.spec:180 [triggers], :186 reload.<conf_file_name> = [ simple |
                 never | rest_endpoints | access_endpoints <handler_url> | http_get
                 <handler_url> | http_post <handler_url> ], :206 "If set to never, Splunk
                 Enterprise initiates a restart after any state change", :212
                 reload.<conf_file_name>.<conf_stanza_prefix>; indexes.conf.spec:800. No
                 condition is written over audit.conf [auditconfig:/path]: that stanza is
                 not declared in the staged specification set, which is stamped Version
                 10.0.0.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: an app.conf [triggers] entry for
                 a configuration file governing the level or type of stored log records is
                 set to "never", so a change to that file requires a restart of the
                 application when the product can apply it in place.
